      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Hypertension is often called \"the silent killer\" because it usually has no symptoms, yet it quietly damages your heart, brain, and kidneys over time. Keeping blood pressure under control is essential to prevent serious conditions like heart attacks, strokes, and severe kidney damage later in life. This guide will help you understand how to manage these numbers safely through simple lifestyle changes and proper medication. True success lies in balancing clear communication with rigorous medical accuracy for lifelong prevention.",
      "source": "target",
